# The export package's proof on this machine: a game booted for play goes
# through the loading page (src/boot/), which lifts off a drawn world that real
# keys then move through. The browser half of the proof is tools/web.sh (title,
# loading page, Enter for a new game, resize, reload) with frames in shots/export/.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/export.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0
# The tour starts with the game's systems, at the page's "start" stage: the page
# is still on the screen while the first frame compiles its shaders. The wait
# covers its "draw" stage and its lift, so the first frame shows the game alone.
echo the game is made under the loading page; waiting for the page to lift
wait 1.5
shot after-the-loading-page
walk 1,0 1.2
walk 0,1 0.8
shot walked-in
tap map
wait 0.4
shot map-of-the-page-island with app:map
tap map
wait 0.3
shot back with app:none
